The plate is likely a side-to-dinner size, with a rim diameter of about 26 cm. The two slices each measure roughly 7 cm by 3 cm, and about 1.5-2 cm thick. That gives about 7 × 3 × 1.8 ≈ 38 cm³ per slice. At a density of about 1 g/cm³, each slice is roughly 40 g, so about 80 g in total.

The slices look like meatloaf or a pâté-style loaf with a ground-meat texture and bits of vegetable. I'd put it at about 220 kcal/100 g.

